{
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "_about": [
    "INCI synonym lexicon. Read by app/services/ingredient_parser.py.",
    "",
    "Maps the names products print on their ingredient lists to the rules",
    "matrix's ingredient keys, and sorts everything else into kinds the",
    "catalogue review can act on. Clinical content, like the matrix (CON-003):",
    "which names count as an ingredient is a judgement, so it lives here,",
    "versioned and reviewable, not in code.",
    "",
    "matrixActives      the matrix's active ingredients, by every printed name.",
    "matrixDerivatives  related forms mapped to a matrix active WITH a warning",
    "                   shown at review: a derivative is not the same molecule,",
    "                   and the reviewer decides whether the rule applies.",
    "nonMatrixActives   actives the matrix does not cover yet. A product",
    "                   containing one is ineligible until the matrix is",
    "                   extended (MVP decision, 2026-10-12): unknown is unsafe.",
    "fragrance          fragrance and the common fragrance allergens. Blocks the",
    "                   'fragrance-free cleanser' step; recorded on every product",
    "                   for the fragrance-allergy filter.",
    "uvFilters, supportive, excipients",
    "                   recognised and inert for matching purposes. Anything the",
    "                   lexicon does not recognise is listed for the reviewer.",
    "excipientPatterns, botanicals  further recognised names (PEG-n, CI colourants, ...).",
    "",
    "Names are lowercase and matched on word boundaries, so 'lactic acid'",
    "does not match 'sodium lactate'."
